Set-list probes now carry collection completeness explicitly. The concrete
browser boundary marks only the exact recovered empty-account state as
`complete`; non-empty My Sets card lists remain `unknown`, and canonical reads
preserve that fact. Differential Create Set verification refuses to capture or
consume a set-list baseline unless the source declares the collection
`complete`. Synthetic complete-list tests preserve the exact-difference verifier
for a future evidence-backed non-empty source; unknown live lists remain
observational only.

My Sets browser reads now tolerate delayed client hydration: after exact route
navigation, the worker retries only the standard page-unavailable envelope for
up to 15 polls within the shared eight-second read deadline. It requires two
identical bounded visible snapshots separated by an event-loop yield, and
rechecks the tab's exact route at each stage. Malformed responses, duplicate
fields, and any insertion, removal, or changed title between snapshots fail
closed before a collection is returned.

The initial and final My Sets snapshots are two observations of one browser
view, not evidence of an atomic server transaction. Only the recovered
empty-account controls can still produce `complete`, and nonempty collections
remain `unknown`; neither snapshot establishes nonempty server completeness.
Synthetic bridge tests cover slow hydration, stable empty accounts, transient
empty-to-nonempty drift, changed cards, and malformed success envelopes.

The worker's initial read-navigation polling now shares its eight-second
request budget with the local five-second navigation limit. The deadline is
captured before `tabs.update`; a late update or delayed `tabs.get` cannot reset
the window or be accepted as a timely completed tab. Both the exact set routes
and route-free session observation use the same admission helper. Synthetic
clock tests cover loaded/loading tabs, stale routes, and browser-call latency;
this does not promise a hung browser API will resolve before its own timeout.

Still pending: non-empty server-side set-list completeness; live browser
acceptance of capability inspection, credential submission, and successful
authenticated navigation; complete question-level media
facts beyond the bounded presence currently observed; the outcome of
