The recovered question form stores correct answers as a list of answer *values*,
not stable row identities. Duplicate serialized answer strings therefore make
row-level correctness ambiguous, even if the visible rows differ by position
or typing match mode. The concrete browser reader and legacy v1 decoder now
reject those inputs rather than marking multiple rows correct. This does not
reject duplicates in already-normalized v2/v3 facts, which contain explicit
per-row correctness and no such provider-value lookup.

The public Blooket identity login page observed on 2026-10-07 exposes the
