Capability inspection cleanup now converts errors from post-close browser
confirmation polls into stable failures, then continues the other cleanup
and original-tab restoration. Synthetic Chrome exceptions verify that a
failed capability probe cannot abandon the tab or return a snapshot.
An empty My Sets probe can produce account-dependent capability evidence only
when the source explicitly confirms a `complete` empty collection. An empty
`unknown` list and duplicate set IDs are rejected before selecting a probe set
or opening any Add Question controls.

Portable capability inspection is now implemented behind the existing
`capabilities.inspect` browser bridge command. The worker selects one already
visible My Sets ID, opens Add Question without submitting it, opens only the
Audio drawer, resolves the shared `hasPlus` media gate, verifies cancellation of
